---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { webPageJsonLd } from '../lib/seo';

// All wording from docs/submission-copy-v0.3.md (Sample report).
// The Your Undercurrent excerpt below is hard-coded on purpose (owner-approved exception in
// CLAUDE.md). Never import or read paid content from anywhere for this page.
const path = '/sample-report/';
const title = 'Sample Report: The Gazing Snow Leopard | Harborwish';
const h1 = 'What’s in your Full Report';
const description =
  'See what’s free and what’s inside the Harborwish Full Report, using the Gazing Snow Leopard as an example.';
---

<Base
  title={title}
  description={description}
  canonicalPath={path}
  jsonLd={webPageJsonLd(Astro.site!, path, h1, description)}
>
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>{h1}</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Here’s how a report is laid out, using the Gazing Snow Leopard as an example. Your own report is written for your own mood animal.
    </p>

    <section class="report-block">
      <h2>Free with every result</h2>
      <p class="report-animal"><strong>The Gazing Snow Leopard</strong> — <em>Sees everything, touches nothing.</em></p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Your Six Dimensions.</strong> Where this mood animal sits on each of the six dimensions, in plain words.</li>
        <li><strong>Your Portrait.</strong> A few paragraphs that try to say what it’s like to be this mood animal right now.</li>
        <li><strong>The Animals Nearest You.</strong> The two mood animals closest on the map, and the one difference between you.</li>
        <li><strong>A gentle note for harder days,</strong> where it fits.</li>
      </ul>
      <p><a href="/animals/snow-leopard/">Read the free Snow Leopard chapter</a></p>
    </section>

    <section class="report-block report-block--paid">
      <h2>Inside the Full Report — $9.99, one time</h2>
      <p>More chapters and a closer read, written for your mood animal:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Your Undercurrent.</strong> What’s moving beneath the surface, in the part of you other people don’t usually see.</li>
        <li><strong>Your Relationships.</strong> How this way of feeling shapes the way you hold on to people, step back from them, or reach for them.</li>
        <li><strong>Your Trap.</strong> The loop this state tends to keep you in, and why it makes so much sense from the inside.</li>
        <li><strong>Your Way Out.</strong> One honest direction to try next, small enough to actually take.</li>
        <li><strong>Your Intensity.</strong> How deeply this mood animal runs in you right now: a light, medium, or deep version of the same animal, with a closer read of each of the six dimensions.</li>
      </ul>

      <p><em>A short excerpt from Your Undercurrent, the first chapter of the Full Report (The Gazing Snow Leopard):</em></p>
      <blockquote class="excerpt">
        <p>Everyone around you thinks you’ve “come through it” — thinks you’ve made your peace, sorted it out, reconciled with yourself. Because what they see is that pairing of low energy and control: no drama, no tears, no scene. You look like someone who lost with perfect grace — stood up from the table, shook hands, smiled, walked out. Flawless composure. So everyone quietly assumes you’re fine. But you know the truth: you didn’t let it go — you filed it.</p>
      </blockquote>
      <p><em>If this feels close to home, the free chapter ends with a note for harder days.</em></p>
    </section>

    <h2>How you get it</h2>
    <p>
      After you buy, we email you a private link. Open it on any device and read whenever you like. There’s nothing to install, no account to create, and no subscription.
    </p>
    {/* Not clickable and not linked anywhere until checkout launches. */}
    <span class="button button--disabled" aria-disabled="true">Launching soon</span>
    <p class="small-print">The Full Report is for self-reflection. It isn’t a diagnosis or professional advice.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
